# component: sheet
# decisions: A11Y-9, API-21, DOC-1, DOC-2, OVL-13, OVL-16, VOI-1
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: `SheetPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class.
#   A11Y-9: `SheetContent` mirrors Base UI's `data-base-ui-inert` markers onto native `inert`
#     through `useModalInert`, gated on the root's `modal` prop published through a context —
#     the same pair `dialog` carries, because upstream's Sheet IS Base UI's Dialog.
#   OVL-16 (widened by MK 2026-09-24, Regent #138): `SheetContent` takes
#     `size?: "sm" | "default" | "lg" | "xl"` (default `"default"`) and reflects it as `data-size`.
#     A left or right sheet steps Dialog's exact scale — `sm:max-w-xs` · `sm:max-w-sm` (upstream's,
#     unchanged) · `sm:max-w-2xl` · `sm:max-w-5xl` — through `data-[side=…]:data-[size=…]` classes,
#     so top and bottom sheets ignore the axis. Below `sm` a side sheet is full width
#     (`data-[side=…]:w-full`), keeping upstream's `w-3/4` from `sm` up.
#   API-21: `SheetBody` (`min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto px-4`) scrolls between the header and the
#     `mt-auto` footer inside the panel's flex column; the panel has no padding of its own, so the
#     body takes none of Dialog's `-mx-4`. `SheetAction` is an end seat in `SheetHeader`
#     (CardAction's grid placement, `me-8` to clear the corner close); the header becomes a
#     two-column grid only while it holds one. `closeLabel` renames the corner close control.
#   VOI-1: the corner close's built-in string is the overridable `closeLabel` (default "Close").
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
